{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Living the Dream"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "A New Hope "}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 16}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le16ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pumped up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "motivated; excited"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That job seminar has me so pumped up right now!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob02aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use after visiting a seminar."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "superfluous"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not necessary"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  The instructor implied that cover letters were superfluous."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob02aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sell yourself"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "convince people that you are able to do something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I feel that a cover letter gives you a chance to sell yourself and explain what you will bring to the table."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob02aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "capabilities"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "abilities; what you are capable of doing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The employer must be sold on your capabilities."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob02aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cut to the chase"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "go directly to the point"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm going to cut to the chase, and explain why I'm writing to them. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob02aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "objectives"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "goals; targets"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I am customizing my cover letter explaining all the different ways that I can meet the company's objectives. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob02aud02"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Passive Voice with Modals"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">passive voice</span> when you want to focus on the receiver of the action, rather than the \u2018doer' of the action.  You can also use<span class=\"strong\"> modal verbs </span> in the <span class=\"strong\">passive voice</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Sometimes, something must/can/should be done by someone. It that case, we use some<span class=\"strong\"> modal verbs</span>. Remember, after a <span class=\"strong\">modal verb</span>, \"to\" is no necessary before the main verb. <br> Example: <span class=\"italic\">This lesson must be practiced. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Modal verbs</span> can add meaning connected with <span class=\"underline\">suggestion</span> or <span class=\"underline\">obligation</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Here is the structure of a <span class=\"strong\">passive</span> sentence:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Subject + modal verb + be + past participle of the main verb"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">All the things I learned there <span class=\"strong\">should be implemented </span>into my job search.</span> <br/><span class=\"italic\">The employer <span class=\"strong\">must be sold</span> on your capabilities.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">A cover letter <span class=\"strong\">has to be done</span>.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">They <span class=\"strong\">have to be sent</span> by Tuesday.</span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">subject</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">have/has/ must</span>\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">past participle</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A cover letter</br> They\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"has </br>  have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to be </br> to be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"done.</br>sent by Tuesday.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The employer\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"must\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sold.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I believe a cover letter has to be done and that it is a big part of the process."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The organization should be complimented."}, {"type": "example", "content": "All the things I learned there should be implemented into my job search."}, {"type": "example", "content": "My instructor at the seminar suggested that a cover letter didn't have to be included with your resume. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Future Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use four different tenses to talk about the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about a things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span> ."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">be going to</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future, you use the Present Continuous tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about schedules, you use the Simple Present. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Will </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I'll talk to you later. </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Be going to </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I am going to send out five resumes. </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Present Continuous </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I'm starting work on monday. </br> I'm interviewing for a job at 2 p.m. tomorrow. </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Simple Present </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Class starts at 7:00 p.m. </span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'll have to make this short."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I am going to write a cover letter, for a company I'm curious about called BFP."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I am customizing my cover letter explaining all the different ways that I can meet the company's objectives. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "  My class starts in five minutes. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of skills and experiences you have."}, {"typ