e to be included with your resume. I disagreed with him, interrupting politely of course, and we debated it, but by the end, he still implied that cover letters were superfluous.", "id": 1}, {"time": "35000", "image": "engenn9le16ob02re2img06.jpg", "text": "Nevertheless, I believe a cover letter has to be done and that it is a big part of the process.  For me, the cover letter comes first, then the resume and finally the interview.\nI feel that a cover letter gives you a chance to sell yourself and explain what you will bring to the table. The employer must be sold on your capabilities.", "id": 2}, {"time": "57000", "image": "engenn9le16ob02re2img07.jpg", "text": "So today, I am going to write a cover letter, for a company I'm curious about called BFP.\nFirst, I'm going to cut to the chase, and  explain why I'm writing to them. Next, the organization should be complimented. I am going to tell BFP why I like them and want to join their organization. Then, I am customizing my cover letter, explaining all the different ways that I can meet the company's objectives. Finally, in my conclusion, I will point out my enthusiasm for the position and how much I want to meet with them and just like that, I'm finished.<br /><br />\nOops. My class starts in five minutes. Got to go.", "id": 3}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}]}]}